There are two words involved here; 'fey' ("doomed to die, accursed,
feeble"; later (C19) "unearthly" by association with the other word),
also spelt at times 'fay'; and 'fay' ("fairy"), also spelt at times
'faye'. Morgan is definitely the latter of these.

(The OED isn't aware of a variant 'fae'; I suspect it's a modernism
influenced by 'faerie')

